WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.076
[MUSIC]

00:00:07.076 --> 00:00:11.062
If an applicant does get an interview,
how would you recommend they prepare for

00:00:11.062 --> 00:00:11.963
that interview?

00:00:11.963 --> 00:00:15.584
&gt;&gt; Well, first of all, if an applicant
gets an interview, congratulations.

00:00:15.584 --> 00:00:16.671
[LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; That's a really good sign [INAUDIBLE]

00:00:16.671 --> 00:00:17.374
[CROSSTALK]
&gt;&gt; Yeah,

00:00:17.374 --> 00:00:21.194
we usually interview about two
candidates for every spot that we have.

00:00:21.194 --> 00:00:24.288
So number one,
the word prepare is a really good one.

00:00:24.288 --> 00:00:28.017
If you've made it this far,
and worked this hard,

00:00:28.017 --> 00:00:31.507
treat this as an important
part of the process.

00:00:31.507 --> 00:00:34.212
Unlike some other schools,
we use our alumni for interviewers, and

00:00:34.212 --> 00:00:35.433
they are all around the globe.

00:00:35.433 --> 00:00:39.421
We try to match you with people from
your country, maybe perhaps an industry

00:00:39.421 --> 00:00:43.493
that you're in if possible, currently in,
so they really understand you.

00:00:43.493 --> 00:00:44.507
And it's in two parts.

00:00:44.507 --> 00:00:47.473
The first half an hour
is primarily evaluative.

00:00:47.473 --> 00:00:49.796
And then the last 15
minutes it's a chance for

00:00:49.796 --> 00:00:51.782
you to meet someone from the community.

00:00:51.782 --> 00:00:55.854
So come prepared with
the mindset to do both.

00:00:55.854 --> 00:00:59.512
And the first part we're going to be
it's a behavioral based interview, so

00:00:59.512 --> 00:01:03.121
the stories that we were talking about
before, come ready to tell them.

00:01:03.121 --> 00:01:06.002
We're going to, want to know
about what you're most proud of.

00:01:06.002 --> 00:01:06.962
What was the context?

00:01:06.962 --> 00:01:08.076
What was the challenge?

00:01:08.076 --> 00:01:09.147
What did you do?

00:01:09.147 --> 00:01:10.386
How did you do it?

00:01:10.386 --> 00:01:12.163
And then what was the impact?

00:01:12.163 --> 00:01:15.818
So expect some probing
around those stories.

00:01:15.818 --> 00:01:18.167
And then on the second part, it's fun.

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:19.136
Our community's so tight.

00:01:19.136 --> 00:01:21.032
[LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; I enjoyed my interview a lot, actually.

00:01:21.032 --> 00:01:22.471
&gt;&gt; Actually?
&gt;&gt; I had a great time.

00:01:22.471 --> 00:01:23.088
&gt;&gt; Yeah.

00:01:23.088 --> 00:01:24.987
And did you enjoy the interviewer?

00:01:24.987 --> 00:01:27.835
&gt;&gt; I did, it's pretty expert, actually.

00:01:27.835 --> 00:01:32.530
It's really good at really drawing
stories out of me rather kind of in like

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:33.903
intense questions.

00:01:33.903 --> 00:01:37.418
And by the end of it, I felt that there
was somebody that I'd really got to know.

00:01:37.418 --> 00:01:39.840
And somebody who was part of a community
I was excited to be a part of.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.332
So the interview was actually really great
for me and getting excited for school.

00:01:44.332 --> 00:01:48.178
&gt;&gt; And that's a wonderful way
to help with the second tip.

00:01:48.178 --> 00:01:50.184
That last part of the interview,
it's a gift.

00:01:50.184 --> 00:01:52.361
It's a chance to develop a relationship.

00:01:52.361 --> 00:01:56.856
Come prepared with some questions that you
want to know about Stanford, obviously,

00:01:56.856 --> 00:02:00.480
but see it as just one entry step to
being part of a bigger community.

